d heads keep the target unknown; a Native source query independently requires its authentic original head receipt. Logical commands with an actual retained source point use Conditional dispatch advice. Nested declaration-only commands use original Lowerer-stamped tokens and the explicit Logical declaration-target projection under the same complete source input, configuration, Registry, vector and declaration-world guards. Their potential source correspondence does not change an absent runtime lookup into Conditional or Reached dispatch; raw targets remain empty and unknown. Neither purpose supplies a Native handler, compiler admission, entered frame, variable execution policy or original Native head receipt.",
