+      "problem_statement": "Source filenames have separate original counted String bytes, external filesystem bytes and diagnostic C-string extents. Conflating those extents, borrowing source script codecs or forgiving strict conversion units changes the selected file and winning result.",
+      "question": "How do the original C and Jim source commands convert counted filename bytes, select real byte-named files and report literal/modified-zero and surrogate-unit failures under actual UTF-8, ISO-8859-1 and identity system encoding selections? What exact results, errorCode, effects, selection results and original headers remain?",
